    "narrative": "For tonight's slate, **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) and **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47) anchor the lineup as our most efficient plays. **Lawrence Butler** earns his elite status by leading off against a moderate arm in Lowder, benefiting significantly from a +18% SP skill boost and a +10% order bonus. Meanwhile, **Jonathan Aranda** exploits a favorable matchup against Sugano; his score is propped up by a strong +19% SP skill advantage and a combined +26% bonus from park and platoon splits. **Bryce Harper** (69.09) and **Daulton Varsho** (67.93) remain essential starts, both capitalizing on favorable platoon dynamics against Irvin and Taillon, respectively. **JJ Bleday** (66.17) rounds out our top-tier group, as the platoon advantage against the lefty Lopez provides a massive +14% lift, pushing him firmly into the strong start category.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer involved **Braden Montgomery** (46.78), who ultimately hit the bench despite a favorable park factor. While his score was respectable, he fell just short of the efficiency threshold required to displace the higher-floor projections of our middle-infield options. We are also monitoring **Jeremiah Jackson** (44.09), who carries a marginal score and a 36% rain risk; while he remains in the lineup due to his park factor, he is a primary candidate for a mid-game swap if weather conditions deteriorate. We have opted to bench **Gleyber Torres** (39.90) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (37.73) due to their inability to clear the 40.0 baseline, prioritizing the higher-upside matchups for **Luis Arraez** (60.13) and **Kyle Karros** (63.20). Despite the volatility, our roster holds a solid concentration of speed and high-contact profiles, which remains our primary lever to gain ground in the SB category while we chase efficiency from **Cal Raleigh** (41.82) and **Brendan Donovan** (41.67) at the bottom of the order.",
